mpp for Ubuntu Rock 5B
----------------------

This source package uses `3.0 (quilt)` but carries **no source patches**. The
upstream delta lives on a fork branch instead, so `debian/patches/` is
deliberately absent.

Source: branch `ysp/main` of https://github.com/yisding/mpp, based on upstream
release tag `1.0.12` (commit 1375813c, 2026-05-29). The branch carries the ysp
delta as reviewable commits:

* osal/test: pthread start routine signature for newer GCC/glibc
* hal/rkenc: harden the vepu5xx encoder slice poll loops against poll failure
* hal/h264e: poll cfg allocation size, and drop the single-cfg reg_idx indexing

The `+ds` orig tarball is exported from that branch tip with the upstream
`debian/` directory and unused Windows binaries removed:

* tools/AStyle.exe
* tools/TextEncoding.exe

Ubuntu packaging changes live under `debian/`.

To add a change, commit it on `ysp/main`, push, then update MPP_COMMIT and
MPP_UPSTREAM_VERSION in packaging/ppa/build-source-packages.sh and rebuild with
FORCE_ORIG=1. Do not reintroduce `debian/patches/` — see
packaging/userspace-patches.md for why this component uses the fork-branch
model.
